From 2223db46eee23cd6f09207f653df8dd46bf362e8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mminin <mminin2010@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 12:59:25 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] XFA: Take picture symbols from the form's locales; add time
 pictures

Default patterns and names were hard-coded for English as in the US, and
French. Canadian English forms then showed date.short{} dates as M/D/YY
instead of their locale's DD/MM/YY. Forms define their locales in a
localeSet packet: read it, on top of built-in definitions for en_US,
en_CA, fr_CA and fr_FR, and use its month, day, meridiem and era names,
date, time and number patterns, and number and currency symbols. Locale
number patterns show one group of digits, so widen them to take large
values.

An empty null{} alternative showed every value as it was, so pictures
such as null{}|num{$z,zzz,zz9.zz} never formatted numbers. null{} now
applies only to null values and zero{} only to zero.

Add time{} and datetime{} pictures, with every hour symbol, minutes,
seconds, thousandths, meridiems and zones as names (GMT, EST...) or
offsets, and classify pictures without a category as numbers, dates,
times or text from their symbols, as FormCalc's Format() and Parse()
need.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
